{"name":"Crocodile Dreams","hex":"#cadabd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crocodile","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the predatory amphibious reptiles of the family Crocodylidae;  a crocodilian, any species of the order Crocodilia, which also includes the alligators, caimans and gavials.","A long line or procession of people (especially children) walking together."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To speak another language than Esperanto at an Esperanto-language gathering."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocodile"},{"term":"dreams","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dream"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of dream"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dreams"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocodile","blocks":[{"text":"A crocodile or true crocodile is a large, semiaquatic reptile that lives throughout the tropics in Africa, Asia, the Americas and Australia. The term \"crocodile\" is sometimes used more loosely to include all extant members of the order Crocodilia, which includes the alligators and caimans, the gharial and false gharial as well as other extinct taxa. This article uses \"crocodile\" or \"true crocodile\" to refer only to the species taxonomically included in the Crocodylidae family, extant or extinct."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Nile_crocodile_head.jpg/330px-Nile_crocodile_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile"},{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/